name: sim.getObject
description: Retrieves an object handle based on its path and alias
luaSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.getObject(string objectPath, dict options = {})
pythonSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.getObject(string objectPath, table options = {})
inputs:
1. objectPath: path and alias of the object to find. See the section on accessing scene objects for details.
2. options: optional map indicating how the object should be searched:
    - noError(bool): can generate a silent error if an object was not found
    - index(int): fetches the n-th object (zero based index) that satisfies the specified objectPath
    - proxy(int):allows to search the hierarchy tree of the specified proxy object
outputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of object or -1
